(Two cases codegen resolves differently: a function-local buffer lives in
 that frame's own stack slot, and a global buffer read from inside a
 function is reached through its BSS mirror (`self.variables` resets per
 function, so `local` resolves via `get_var`; `shared` only resolves via
 `global_var_label`). `Free` has to walk both paths, exactly like
 `BufferClear`/`BufferResize` already do.)

a buffer called shared is "outer".

To 'scratch work'.
    a buffer called local is "inner".
    Free local.
    Print "local len {local's length}".

To 'discard shared'.
    Free shared.

'scratch work'.
'discard shared'.
Print "shared len {shared's length}".
